            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>A user equipment (DUE1) configured for a communication in a wireless communication system, the wireless communication system comprising a plurality of user equipments (DUE1, DUE2, ΔUE1, ΔUE2) and a plurality of transmission/reception points, TRPs, (300, 302), the plurality of TRPs including at least a first TRP (300) and a second TRP (302) and forming a coordinated multipoint, CoMP, cluster serving an area (A) in which the plurality of user equipments (DUE1, DUE2, ΔUE1, ΔUE2) are located, andwherein the user equipment (DUE1) is assigned to a group (310) of user equipments, the group (310) including- two or more user equipments (DUE1, ΔUE1) for which second order channel statistics for the channel between the first and second TRPs (300, 302) and the user equipment are within a certain range, or- two or more user equipments (DUE1, ΔUE1) which are within a certain geographical area relative to the first and second TRPs (300, 302),wherein the user equipment (DUE1) is configured to communicate with the first and second TRPs (300, 302) using the first resources (R1), the first resources (R1) being orthogonal to second resources (R2) used by another user equipment (ΔUE1) of the group (310), andwherein, for transmitting or receiving data for the user equipment (DUE1), the user equipment (DUE1) is configured to- transmit to or receive from the first TRP (300) a first superimposed signal using the first resources (R1) and including a data signal of the user equipment (□UE1) superimposed with a data signal of a further user equipment (□UE2) in a further group (312), and- transmit to or receive from the second TRP (302) a second superimposed signal using the first resources (R1) and including a further data signal of the further user equipment (□UE2) superimposed with a further data signal of the user equipment (□UE1).</p>
            </abstract>
